WEBVTT

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:26.310
"Bottom-Tier Character Tomozaki"

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:40.140
"August Dessert Menu"

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.510
"August Dessert Menu"
"Sweet-Bean Matcha Shaved Ice"
"Lemon Shaved Ice"

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:43.520
Thank you for your patience.
"Bonus Lv. 2:
Post-game equipment for girls
is a little different than usual"

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.680
Your honey-lemon shaved ice
"Bonus Lv. 2:
Post-game equipment for girls
is a little different than usual"

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.400
and sweet-bean matcha shaved ice.
"Bonus Lv. 2:
Post-game equipment for girls
is a little different than usual"

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.400
Relax and enjoy!

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:58.740
She was super cute, right?

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:01.620
I thought so, too! Super cute!

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.160
You can go on break now, Fuka.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:07.790
All right.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.840
It looks like Nakagawa's
prepping a kitchen order,

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:17.470
so I'll get that delivered,
<i>then </i>take my break.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:18.760
Oh, would you?

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:21.640
That'd be a big help, Kikuchi.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.930
All set. Could you run that out for me?

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:25.140
Sure.

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:30.560
Kikuchi's so cute--and such a nice girl.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.820
She really is. And <i>way </i>out of your league.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:36.820
Yeah, you wouldn't stand a chance.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:39.860
Wow, boss--rude!

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:42.320
Okay, I'll go on break now.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:43.280
Got it.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:44.790
Enjoy!

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.920
"Summer's almost over, huh"
"Fumiya Tomozaki: It went by
in the blink of an eye"

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.170
"It really did"
"BTW, I finished <i>Kind Dogs Stand Alone</i>!
Let me know when you're done--
I want to talk about it with you"

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:00.130
"Ichibangai"

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:02.300
Let's see...

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:05.220
It's so hot. Our ice cream's gonna melt.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.270
We haven't even bought any yet!

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:10.850
Oh, I think it's up ahead.

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:12.900
We made it!

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.980
Isn't this...?

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:18.690
Hey, what if Kikuchi's working today?

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:24.120
Given her personality,
she may be overly polite.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.240
I can see that, yeah.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:27.790
All riiight! Let's head on in!

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:29.620
C'mon, Fumiya.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.750
R-Right.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:39.880
He never did write back...

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:47.180
To-Tomozaki?!

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:53.770
And a bunch of people from our class!

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:55.270
What's up?

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:59.400
Wow, I've never heard you be that loud!

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.240
You must have been really startled.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.410
Um... I was.

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:08.290
I guess Kikuchi... isn't here today?

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:11.000
What's up, Fumiya?

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.580
Jeez, did I startle you that much?

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:15.580
You don't have to be so loud.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:19.130
You sure are acting weird, Tomozaki.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:21.010
Why, you...

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.550
Mmm, how to choose...

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:28.140
Does everyone know what they're getting?

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:30.140
Yep. I do.

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:32.100
I've decided, too.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.730
So have I--I think.

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:35.690
You <i>know </i>I've got it <i>down</i>!

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:39.320
What? Everyone but me?! Hang on a second!

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.940
Hurry up or it'll get cold.

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:45.280
Hey! We don't even have
any of our food yet!

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:46.820
Oh, right.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.460
Oh, I get it now.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:57.380
That's fine. I'll take
that half of the floor,

00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:59.590
and you can take the other half.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:01.710
Is that okay with you, boss?

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:04.840
Sure. You're a good worker, after all.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:07.010
Thank you so much.

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:11.560
Her classmates are here, eh?

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:13.600
That Fuka's a shy one.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:14.850
She sure is.

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:18.020
What if one of them is a boy she likes?

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.730
Wh-What, <i>Fuka</i>?!

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:23.690
That's one huge overreaction, boss.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:26.030
And he bought us a matching pair.

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:29.160
Afterwards, we rode the Ferris wheel--

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.660
Here we go! The Ferris wheel!

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.450
Ooh! Can it be?

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:34.200
Did Shuji finally...?

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:39.330
Nothing happened, and the ride ended.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:41.750
No way! Make a move, Shuji!

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:43.880
Right? Right?!

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:46.300
Still, I saw <i>that </i>coming.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:47.930
T-Totally.

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:52.510
Did he not start dating right away
when he was with Shimano?

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:56.730
He saw his chance and wound up
going for it pretty quickly, yeah.

00:05:56.730 --> 00:05:58.560
I thought so!

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:02.190
Maybe Shuji just isn't
interested in me after all.

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:07.030
Mmm, I think he's acting like this
<i>because </i>he likes you.

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:09.950
He really cares, so he
doesn't want to hurt you.

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:11.660
Y-Yeah, I get that.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:13.410
R-Really?

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.910
I think you can breathe easy.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:17.620
Oh, okay.

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:20.420
Well, all right. If you say so.

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:24.090
Honestly. You two are both
as naïve as each other.

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:25.460
You hush!

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:29.340
You don't even <i>have</i>
a special someone, Hiro!

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:31.680
Who, me? I sure do.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:40.650
You don't even <i>have</i>
a special someone, Hiro!

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:43.400
A-A special someone?

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:49.570
I-I shouldn't!

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:52.320
This is basically eavesdropping!

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:54.240
Order up!

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.660
Wh-What's this?

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:01.920
A cheese-stuffed Hamburg steak
with cheese sauce.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:05.300
Someone must <i>really </i>like cheese, huh?

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:08.130
This is probably Hinami's!

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:11.680
What?! You <i>do </i>have someone
you like, Hiro? What's she like?

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:13.510
Hmm, good question.

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:15.510
I am <i>dying </i>of curiosity over here!

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:17.520
Yeah, I'm crazy curious myself!

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:19.100
You can say that again.

00:07:20.350 --> 00:07:22.020
Well, you know...

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:24.520
We can talk and talk
and she stays mysterious--

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:28.780
and before I knew it, she had me
in the palm of her hand.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:32.200
Oh, come on, you big tease! Is she older?

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:33.820
Nope, our age.

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:35.950
Huh!

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:38.450
A girl our age, and you're
wrapped around her little finger?

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:40.330
I wonder what she's like?

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:42.170
I can't even imagine!

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:45.630
Th-That's right. Can't even imagine.

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:48.800
Right? Plus, she's such a hard worker--

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.510
Thank you for your patience!

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:54.600
Who had the cheese-stuffed
Hamburg steak with cheese sauce?

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:56.390
Me!

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:04.900
And when she happens to smile,
it's so innocent and charming.

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:06.520
Like that.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:07.940
Oh, really?

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:10.440
Well, gee, that's fantastic!

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:14.030
Whoa!

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:15.120
Seriously?

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:18.830
So everyone at that table
is a classmate of yours?

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:21.540
Th-That's right.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:24.830
That sure is a bunch of
good-looking people, though.

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:26.880
Y-You think so?

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:30.210
Oh, but maybe not that one guy.

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:34.220
Yeah, that guy's more burly than handsome.

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:37.010
That... that would be Takei.

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:39.720
Yummo!

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:48.480
Man, that was <i>delicious</i>!

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:49.940
It really was!

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:52.110
This was fun!

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:54.450
You do appreciate a good love-life chat.

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:57.450
We heard all kinds of
interesting tidbits today, right?

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:58.990
Right!

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:02.080
Man, I wish <i>I </i>had a love life!

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:04.250
All right, then: shall we?

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:05.420
Okay!

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:08.340
Where to next, gang?

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:14.260
Nice work today, Fuka.

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:17.220
Thank you. I'll be leaving now.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:18.470
See you later!

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:19.970
Good job!

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:23.350
I know I caused a lot of problems
for everyone today.

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:27.900
No, not at all. You're always
a soothing presence around here.

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:29.270
Exactly right.

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:31.650
Good thing they didn't spot you!

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:33.360
Right!

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:40.160
<i>Was </i>it a good thing?

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:45.580
It's almost like there's a whole other
world out there that isn't mine.

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:48.920
But I chose to avoid it.

00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:57.630
"I should be done reading it tonight,
so let's discuss our takes on it tomorrow!
And hey, weren't you at your
job around noon today?"

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:07.140
"Tomozaki,"

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:09.650
"Tomozaki,
you always manage to find me"

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:12.610
"Tomozaki,
you always manage to find me"

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:16.360
"And hey, weren't you at your
job around noon today?"

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:18.490
"Yes, I was. You could tell, huh?"
"And hey, weren't you at your
job around noon today?"
